{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113495-how-could-the-garou-do-interrogations","id":1113495,"title":"How could the garou do interrogations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-08T19:01:01-07:00","id":1113495,"title":"How could the garou do interrogations?","content":"I am thinking about getting W20 and am already thinking up a storyline involving Nigerian scammers. In one part of this prospective storyline, they kidnap a British account named Simon Cogswell, a associate of the scammers and try to shake him down for info. My question is, what type of tricks could Garou use for interrogations and how well can they do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:11:42-07:00","id":1113616,"title":"","content":"1) Garou are great at intimidation. Even without investing in social traits, they can use Rage instead (though Frenzy can be an issue).<br /> <br /> 2) The Persuasion Gift (Rank 1) makes things pretty easy unless there's supernatural defenses against such things on the target's behalf.<br /> <br /> 3) Garou have social pack tactics to use to make these all even easier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T23:52:16-07:00","id":1113628,"title":"","content":"While it might endanger the veil if you plan on letting the target go, you could tie the person up and transform into Crinos form in front of him. Doing this would be supernaturally terrifying and can be done indefinitely. Shift and scare the crap out of the guy, then change back, then shift into Crinos again, and then change back. Depending in the Willpower of the victim, he might forget why he's so terrified as soon as you take human form again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:40:40-07:00","id":1113857,"title":"","content":"Glabro is usually pretty physically intimidating in itself.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good Cop and Bad Cop left for the day. (*growls*) I'm a completely different kind of cop.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: IIRC, Galliards have a couple of Gifts that are useful for playing with people's heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T06:01:08-07:00","id":1114126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113495-how-could-the-garou-do-interrogations?p=1113857#post1113857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: IIRC, Galliards have a couple of Gifts that are useful for playing with people's heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Dreamspeak is a fantastic Interrogation Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T21:54:15-07:00","id":1120232,"title":"","content":"I remember the scene from The Princess Bride when the good guys are storming the castle...<br /> <br /> &quot;Give us the gate key.&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no gate key.&quot;<br /> &quot;Fezzik, tear his arms off.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh you mean this gate key.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:23:16-07:00","id":1121049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113495-how-could-the-garou-do-interrogations?p=1120232#post1120232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember the scene from The Princess Bride when the good guys are storming the castle...<br /> <br /> &quot;Give us the gate key.&quot;<br /> &quot;I have no gate key.&quot;<br /> &quot;Fezzik, tear his arms off.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh you mean this gate key.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound like something a Garou would threaten to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T05:16:55-07:00","id":1124704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113495-how-could-the-garou-do-interrogations?p=1121049#post1121049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does sound like something a Garou would threaten to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would they be strong enough? I mean completely tearing someone's arms off, both at the same time? Even in Crinos, with a base Strength of 5... there are a lot of ligaments, lots of connective tissue, the rotator cuff muscles; it's not just something you could do with (say) Strength 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:29:19-07:00","id":1124792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1113495-how-could-the-garou-do-interrogations?p=1124704#post1124704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would they be strong enough? I mean completely tearing someone's arms off, both at the same time? Even in Crinos, with a base Strength of 5... there are a lot of ligaments, lots of connective tissue, the rotator cuff muscles; it's not just something you could do with (say) Strength 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is more of the threat of it happening and the fear of the would be victim to it actually failing that would be effective. Anyways, if some guy turns into a giant werewolf and I don't fall into delirium I would definitely believe it possible and won't start thinking in the anatomical possibilities (or impossibilities) of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:52:17-07:00","id":1124835,"title":"","content":"&quot;Wishboning&quot; enemies is a legitimate attack in combat, so I believe it should be a credible threat. Are you, as a mortal human, going to look a big, ugly, ragey glabro in the eyes and not take the threat seriously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}